  "reason": "The records provide separate ingredients pointing in the right direction: the starting FCC/B2 lamellar constitution and its soft/hard-phase deformation behavior are established for closely related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni eutectic alloys; pressure and combined pressure-temperature treatments are known to transform HEA structures; and R6 directly establishes that coherent interfaces can transmit dislocations and relieve crack-producing stress concentrations. Other records support the contribution of stacking faults, twins, transformations, and multiple deformation modes to strength-ductility synergy. However, no record applies HPHT to the Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellar alloy or predicts that it will create the specific hierarchical coherent FCC/B2 architecture. R6 also concerns coherent precipitates in a refractory HEA and expressly limits extension to brittle B2-containing systems. Thus an expert could identify a plausible direction, but selecting hexahedron-anvil HPHT and anticipating the reported structural transformation would require a substantial new idea."
